    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are delighted to present to the market 23 Auburn House. A wonderful opportunity to acquire a turn key, 3 bedroom duplex apartment within the mature residential development off Upper Rathmines Road. \r\n\r\nThe apartment has been wonderfully refurbished in recent years with bright interiors with elegant proportions. Seldom does an apartment of this size and quality come to the market with the additional benefit of secure parking across the street. \r\n\r\nThe internal accommodation briefly comprises of entrance hallway with understairs storage. Spacious open plan dining/living area with floor to ceiling window, feature fireplace and opening to kitchen off. The kitchen has a wide range of shaker style units and breakfast bar seating. The first of three bedrooms is also at this level.  \r\n\r\nUpstairs on the landing is the hotpress and skylight. Bedroom 2 is to the rear which is currently in use a walk in wardrobe and bedroom 3 also to the rear has a very practical walk in wardrobe off. The shower room completes the internal accommodation with large walk in shower, w.c and whb. \r\n\r\nThis is a very convenient location with the city centre less than a 15 minute walk away. The LUAS is within walking distance along with a number of regular bus routes linking into the city and further afield. \r\n\r\nPositioned off Upper Rathmines Road and within a short stroll brings you to a variety of top restaurants and pubs including Kodiak, Lottie’s, Reggies, The Stella and Elephant & Castle with many more throughout Rathmines. Dunville Avenue and Upper Rathmines Road are home to boutique shops, butchers and delis. Whilst Ranelagh village is less than a 10-minute walk away offering an even further selection of restaurants, bars and cafes."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall \r\nLaminate floor and understairs storage. \r\n\r\nLiving /Dining \r\nHigh quality laminate floor, floor to ceiling window and feature fire.  \r\n\r\nKitchen \r\nAn extensive range of shaker style kitchen units, extractor fan, plumbed for washing machine, recessed lights, laminate floor and island unit with breakfast bar seating. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1 \r\nLaminate floor\r\n\r\nUpstairs\r\nLanding \r\nSkylight and hot press off. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (currently in use as a dressing room)\r\nLaminate floor and walk in wardrobe. \r\n\r\nBedroom 3\r\nLaminate floor and walk in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nBathroom\r\nLarge walk in shower with rainfall and telephone attachment, w.c, whb with vanity backlit mirror above, shelving, tiled floor and walls. \r\n\r\nOutside \r\nSecure parking."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "GFCH \r\nSpacious accommodation \r\nOff street parking\r\nExcellent condition throughout\r\nThree generous bedrooms\r\nSecure parking \r\nManagement fee of € 1,879.95 per annum \r\nGreat transport links into the city centre including LUAS and bus routes\r\nBeside Rathmines and Ranelagh villages\r\nLocal shops on Upper Rathmines Road and Dunville Avenue\r\nBeside several green open spaces and parks \r\nConvenient to the M50 and city centre"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: B3\r\nBER No. 103043964"
      }
    ],
